# E14 Voting: sequential, fixed order; the preferences come from the seed of the oracle, drawn from one generator
# shared by the voters, so the C# fixes every line (exact trace): the 99 votes in the order the teller receives them,
# then the Condorcet winner if there is one, the winner of Copeland's method and the winner of the Borda count.
cover all
fact line ^(.*)$
fact vote ^(\d( \d)*)$
fact verdict ^(Candidate \d is the Condorcet winner|There is no Condorcet winner)$
fact condorcet ^Candidate (\d) is the Condorcet winner$
fact no_condorcet ^There is no Condorcet winner$
fact copeland ^Using Copeland's method, candidate (-?\d+) is the winner$
fact borda ^Using Borda count, candidate (-?\d+) is the winner$
# Whether a Condorcet winner exists depends on the draw (one with the seed of the oracle, none with CAM_SEED=42): one
# verdict either way
optional condorcet
optional no_condorcet
same line seq
same vote seq
same verdict seq
same condorcet seq
same no_condorcet seq
same copeland seq
same borda seq
check vote count == 99
check verdict count == 1
check copeland count == 1
check borda count == 1
